description: UI system rules for production landing pages
globs:
  - "**/*.{html,css,scss,ts,tsx,js,jsx}"
alwaysApply: true
---

# Design System Foundation
- Use a token-first approach for colors, spacing, typography, radius, and shadows.
- Prefer centralized variables over one-off hardcoded values.
- Keep visual language consistent across all sections and components.

# Layout and Grid
- Use mobile-first responsive layout.
- Keep content width constrained with consistent container behavior.
- Maintain predictable vertical rhythm between sections.
- Prefer simple, reusable layout primitives over custom per-section layout logic.

# Typography
- Keep a clear type scale with predictable heading/body hierarchy.
- Use readable line length and line height for long text blocks.
- Avoid decorative typography that reduces clarity.
- Ensure headings communicate meaning, not only style.

# Component Rules
- Build reusable section-level components (hero, cards, FAQ items, CTA blocks, forms).
- Prefer variants for state and context differences instead of duplicate components.
- Keep component APIs explicit and minimal.
- Avoid deeply nested component trees without clear benefit.

# State and Interaction
- Interactive elements must define states: default, hover, active, focus, disabled, loading.
- Focus states must be clearly visible for keyboard users.
- Motion should be subtle and purposeful; avoid distracting animations.
- Respect reduced-motion preferences when adding animations.

# Forms and Inputs
- Keep labels explicit and error text actionable.
- Use consistent spacing and alignment for input groups.
- Do not rely on color alone to communicate validation state.
- Submission feedback must be immediate and clear.

# Media and Imagery
- Use responsive images and avoid oversized assets.
- Keep image framing and aspect-ratio style consistent in galleries/cases.
- Alt text is required for meaningful images.
- Decorative visuals should not compete with primary CTA and content clarity.

# Accessibility Baseline
- Use semantic HTML landmarks and proper heading order.
- Ensure keyboard navigation works end-to-end.
- Maintain color contrast suitable for body text and controls.
- Avoid interaction patterns that depend only on hover.

# Implementation Discipline
- Keep styles modular and close to component boundaries where practical.
- Avoid duplicate style blocks; extract shared utilities when repeated.
- Do not introduce UI libraries unless required by scope.
- Any visual deviation from system tokens should be explicitly justified.

# QA Checklist for UI Changes
- Verify mobile (320+), tablet, and desktop layouts.
- Verify no horizontal overflow in key viewports.
- Verify interactive states are visible and consistent.
- Verify CTA prominence remains strong after UI updates.
